<title>INDIA: Citibank urges Indian rupee money market.</title>
<headline>Citibank urges Indian rupee money market.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A senior executive of Citibank NA on Friday urged India to develop a rupee short-term money market, which he said would help to create a viable bond market.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe that regulatory authorities should start developing a rupee short-term money market by way of a inter-bank placement market,&quot; David Connor, head of Citibank's operations in India, Sri Lanka, Nepal and Bangladesh, said.</p>
<p>&quot;A rupee short-term interbank market will have an impact on creating a viable bond market,&quot; he told a business conference in the Indian capital.</p>
<p>Connor said a more developed bond market would improve debt and liquidity in forward foreign exchange markets.</p>
<p>&quot;Liquidity will improve and there will be an increase in transparency of interest rate and rupee markets,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
